WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
Good to have you on Planetary and Daily, Episode 78 for June 3, 2026.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.040
Some interesting findings to cover today.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:14.440
Childhood flu vaccine analysis shows 9-14 fewer influenza cases per 100 children aged 2-5.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.880
A study separating industrial from ruminant derived trans fats found the latter,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:25.580
present in milk, butter, and cheese, did not elevate cardiovascular or metabolic risk.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.760
The distinction arises because dairy trans fats are produced by microbial fermentation in the

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.820
rumin rather than industrial hydrogenation. Population level intake data were matched

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.740
against disease incidence records to reach this conclusion. Nutrition labels that list partially

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:49.540
hydrogenated oils therefore point to a different category than the ruminant trans fats in dairy products.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.980
Now, shifting to a very different area of research. A new meta-analysis examined vaccine

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:03.080
impact across multiple seasons for children aged 2-5. For every 100 vaccinated children in this group,

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.320
investigators recorded between 9-14 fewer influenza cases per season.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:14.980
The findings align with earlier observational data but provide tighter bounds on expected population

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:20.680
level effects. Public health agencies can use the numbers to refine school-based vaccination

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:26.760
targets. Electronic health records combined with symptom surveys identified many individuals

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:33.440
meeting long-covid criteria who lack a formal diagnosis. The analysis suggests the true burden

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:40.160
exceeds recorded case counts by a substantial margin. Refined diagnostic criteria and broader

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.800
screening are listed as immediate research priorities. Researchers at the Pontifical Catholic

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:52.340
University of Sao Paulo developed a composite containing jackfruit latex, pomegranate peel extract,

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:58.760
and cymbastatin. In laboratory and animal tests, the material reduced bacterial load and supported

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:05.460
tissue repair in periodontal pockets. The statin component appears to modulate local inflammation while

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:12.000
the plant extracts provide antimicrobial activity. Human pilot studies are the next step outlined by the

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.440
team. A four-year study led by Latrobe University found that hairy scarab beetles use candlestick

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:23.120
bank sea flowers as nocturnal mating sites while feeding on them in large numbers.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.580
The beetle's behavior provides the primary pollination for one of perse most common native trees.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.560
Researchers documented the insects arriving at dusk and remaining through the night.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:40.760
Transferring pollen between plants during mass gatherings. The work reveals an unexpected plant

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:46.440
insect relationship that had not been recorded in prior surveys of Australian pollination systems.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:52.040
Follow-up observations will test whether similar beetle-mediated pollination occurs in other

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:58.620
bank-seas species. Acoustic monitoring across managed forests showed resident species consistently

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:04.440
avoiding areas with heavy clear cutting. The data indicate that retention of older forest patches

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:10.380
supports higher bird occupancy. The findings support calls for modified harvest patterns that

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:17.560
maintain structural diversity within stands. McMaster University researchers working with VU Amsterdam

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:22.940
and the Woodwell Climate Research Center linked shorter snow cover seasons to reduced

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:29.800
albedo benefits from fire-driven landscape change. Earlier snow melt exposes darker surfaces sooner,

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:36.260
offsetting the cooling that followed past fires. The study projects further erosion of this feedback

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:43.280
as northern snow seasons continue to shorten. Cornell scientists created atomic scale moire structures

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:49.000
by applying controlled strain rather than mechanical twisting or stacking. The approach,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:55.160
detailed in proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, yields more uniform patterns over larger

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:01.560
areas. Resulting materials exhibit the same quantum behaviors previously seen only in twisted

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:08.560
bilayer graphene. Scaleability improvements could accelerate device prototyping. A team observed

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:14.600
platinum and nickel atoms separating and reinterfacing within nanoscale particles during operation.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:21.040
The dynamic interface increased electrochemical water splitting activity beyond static alloy

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:27.440
benchmarks. Real-time imaging captured the rearrangement process directly. The work points towards

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.460
synthesis routes that exploit in situ restructuring for other multi-metal catalysts.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:39.640
Male bower birds in an Australian city collected glass, plastic, banknotes, and even a pair of handcuffs

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:45.280
to decorate their twig tunnels. The items were presented to visiting females as part of courtship,

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.640
according to observations published in Royal Society Open Science. Researchers recorded higher

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:57.500
visit rates when displays included brightly colored or reflective objects. The behavior demonstrates

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:03.900
rapid incorporation of novel materials into an existing signaling system. The Greater Amberjack

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:09.960
Count Project, led by Sean P. Powers at the University of South Alabama, combined multiple survey

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:16.160
methods across the South Atlantic and Gulf regions. The resulting data revised prior stock assessments

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:21.920
upward for certain age classes. Fisheries managers will incorporate the figures into the next

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:27.120
quota setting cycle. Additional tagging work is planned to refine movement patterns between

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:33.500
management zones. Fresh evidence compiled from multiple cohorts shows limited additional benefit

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:38.860
beyond the first year. Alongside documented side effects that include sexual dysfunction,

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:45.680
emotional numbing, cognitive slowing, and weight gain. The analysis distinguishes these outcomes

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:51.820
from short-term trial results that formed the original approval data. Clinicians are examining whether

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:57.840
periodic reassessment protocols could reduce cumulative exposure without increasing relapse rates.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:04.500
Researchers tracked waste shipment rerouting from the United States, Netherlands, Australia, and Japan.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.460
To Southeast Asian ports, once Chinese facilities stopped accepting foreign plastic.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:15.040
The diverted material increased open burning and uncontrolled processing in Indonesia,

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:21.600
raising particulate levels in affected regions. The study links the policy shift directly to

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:29.920
measurable changes in local air monitoring data collected after 2018. Analysis of long-term forest

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:36.420
inventory records by Concordia researchers documented increased conifer stem density after decades

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:42.680
of decline. The reversal coincides with changes in harvesting practices and natural regeneration

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:48.200
patterns. Continued monitoring will determine whether the trend persists under current climate

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:52.700
conditions. Data presented at the European Geosciences Union,

00:06:53.640 --> 00:07:00.360
2026, meeting revealed complex topography and compositional heterogeneity across the dwarf planet.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:06.680
Earlier interpretations based on limited fly-by imagery underestimated the range of land forms.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:12.380
Additional orbital or landed measurements would be required to map the newly identified units.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:17.540
You've probably heard that all trans fats raise heart disease risk and should be avoided.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.460
But here's what's actually happening. Right now, as you consider your next meal,

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:28.260
the trans fats in butter or cheese are produced by bacteria inside a cow's room in,

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:34.380
creating a different set of isomers than those formed during industrial partial hydrogenation of

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:40.900
vegetable oils. One memorable distinction is that dairy trans fats show no association with increased

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:47.420
cardiovascular events or type 2 diabetes in large cohort studies, whereas industrial versions do.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:53.960
The next time you see a nutrition label, checking whether partially hydrogenated oils appear in

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:59.840
the ingredient list will tell you which category is present. Next time, we'll be watching for updates

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:05.160
on the greater Amberjack stock assessments and the human pilot studies for the Jack Fruit Latex

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:11.940
Biomaterial. That's Planetarian Daily for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating or review on Apple

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:17.360
podcasts or Spotify really helps new listeners find the show. I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

